## Performance (agent-checkable)

- Route-lazy heavy deps (charts, PDF, xlsx, editors) — do not grow the initial Work-tier bundle with report-only libs.
- Declare size on media/charts to avoid CLS — `mms-ui-ux-design.mdc`.

## MMS edit discipline

1. Read implicated files before editing; validate against `@mms/shared` and `schema.ts`.
2. New UI must be config-driven (field/tab/column registry).
3. Remove unused imports/dead code in the change boundary.
4. Respect file-size bands when touching large files — hard ~300 / soft ~220; split behind stable barrels — `mms-structure-naming.mdc`, `mms-dry.mdc`.
5. Run `pnpm typecheck` after non-trivial changes; completion review per `mms-completion-review.mdc`.
6. Never commit unless the user asks; never commit `.env` or credentials.
7. Do not expand into migration-status open gaps or “Do not reintroduce” items unless the task requires them.

### Anti-patterns

```tsx
// ❌ Nested ContactConfigProvider — mount once in TenantScopedProviders only
<ContactConfigProvider><ContactsPage /></ContactConfigProvider>

// ❌ Frontend importing backend
import { getCollection } from '../../../backend/src/db/database';

// ✅ Shared types
import type { Contact } from '@mms/shared';
```

## Hardcoding ban

No hardcoded user-facing strings, labels, colours, formats, or statuses.

| Kind | Owner |
|------|--------|
| App copy (nav, toasts, modals, settings) | **`mms-settings-i18n.mdc`** — `t('key')` |
| Field/tab/status labels | Registries + `labelKey` / `StatusBadge` — **`mms-fields.mdc`**, **`mms-settings-i18n.mdc`** |
| Theme colours | `branding` / CSS variables — **`mms-ui-ux-design.mdc`** |
| Module prefs & formats | `@mms/shared` `DEFAULT_*` + settings getters — **`mms-settings-i18n.mdc`** |
| Platform apex locale | **English/LTR only** — `shouldForcePlatformEnglish` — **`mms-settings-i18n.mdc`** |
| Platform session | Separate `mms_platform_access` cookie + `/api/platform/auth/*` — **`mms-auth-security.mdc`** (not tenant `mms_access`) |
| Unknown tenant host | Hard-redirect to apex `/tenant-not-found?subdomain=…` — **never** stay on bad host or open `/settings` — **`mms-settings-i18n.mdc`**, **`mms-ui-ux-design.mdc`** §8 |

Contacts legacy `uiStrings` is migration debt — new copy uses `appTranslations` (`mms-migration-status.mdc`).

## Domain

- **Contact-first persons:** `contacts` canonical; module rows link by id; hydrate on read, strip on save.
- **`persona`:** Purged everywhere — residual = migration defect.
- **Phones:** E.164 on save (`parsePhoneNumber` from `@mms/shared`; backend contacts route too).
- **Contact collection deletes:** empty list arrays must persist (no scalar / merge resurrection) — **`mms-form-architecture.mdc`** §3, **`mms-data-layer.mdc`**.
- **Field / tab enablement:** Setup Fields is SSOT — form, drawer, export, and BE validation must respect the same helpers (`resolveContactEnabledTabIds`, locked `basic`+`custom`) — **`mms-fields.mdc`**.
- **WhatsApp:** Only `PuppeteerWhatsAppProvider.getNumberId` — no manual toggles in UI.

## Module pages

Three tiers only — details split by concern:

- **Shell & universal behaviour:** `mms-module-architecture.mdc`
- **Shell components:** `mms-ui-ux-design.mdc` (`useFilteredModuleTierTabs`, `ResponsiveAccordionTabs`, PageHeader)
- **Content scope:** `mms-module-architecture.mdc` (what belongs in `work` / `reports` / `setup`)
